Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `frozen` was consumed by a lambda that captures it, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/frozen_capture_use_after_move.jet:11:18
    |
 11 |     print(frozen.value)
    |                  ^^^^^
  --> tests/ui/frozen_capture_use_after_move.jet:8:21
    |
  8 |         child: task ^frozen { frozen.value }
    |                     ^^^^^^^ `frozen` moved to a lambda that captures it here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `frozen` after the move, or give a lambda that captures it a copy with `frozen.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
